# TrueTalk.Ai Codebase Overview

This document provides a detailed map of the project structure, explaining where key code resides and what each file does.

## 📂 Project Root (`TrueTalk.Ai/`)
This is the main container for your Django project.

-   **[manage.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/manage.py)**: The command-line utility for Django. You use this to run the server (`runserver`), make migrations, and create superusers.
-   **[db.sqlite3](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/db.sqlite3)**: The local database file where all your users, messages, and groups are stored.
-   **`Project/`**: The main configuration folder for the Django project.
    -   **[settings.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/Project/settings.py)**: Contains all global settings (installed apps, database config, `CHANNEL_LAYERS` for WebSockets).
    -   **[asgi.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/Project/asgi.py)**: The entry point for the ASGI server (Daphne). This is **critical** for WebSockets to work. It routes traffic to HTTP or WebSocket consumers.
    -   **[urls.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/urls.py)**: The main URL router. It directs incoming HTTP requests to the appropriate app (e.g., `ChatRoom`).

---

## 🐍 Backend App (`ChatRoom/`)
This app handles the core chat functionality.

### Key Files:
-   **[models.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/models.py)**: Defines the database structure.
    -   [User](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/my-app/src/components/Sidebar.jsx#23-32): (Imported from Django) Stores username/password.
    -   [Group](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/models.py#5-15): Stores group names and members.
    -   [Message](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/models.py#17-53): Stores text, sender, receiver, timestamp, and `is_read` status.
-   **[views.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/views.py)**: Handles HTTP API requests (REST API).
    -   [UserViewSet](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/views.py#19-33): Handles user creation and fetching user lists.
    -   [MessageViewSet](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/views.py#9-12): Fetches message history.
    -   [GroupViewSet](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/views.py#14-17): Handles group creation and listing.
-   **[consumers.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/consumers.py)**: **The Heart of Real-Time Chat**.
    -   [ChatConsumer](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/consumers.py#8-171): A WebSocket consumer that handles:
        -   Connecting users to rooms.
        -   Receiving messages from the frontend.
        -   Saving messages to the database.
        -   Broadcasting messages to other users in the room.
        -   Handling **Read Receipts** ([read_receipt](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/consumers.py#111-117) event).
-   **[routing.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/routing.py)**: Maps WebSocket URLs (e.g., `ws://.../chat/room/`) to the [ChatConsumer](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/consumers.py#8-171).
-   **[serializers.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/serializers.py)**: Converts complex database objects (like [Message](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/models.py#17-53)) into JSON format for the API and WebSockets.

---

## ⚛️ Frontend App (`ChatRoom/my-app/`)
This is the React application that runs in the browser.

### Key Directories:
-   **`src/`**: Source code folder.
    -   **`main.jsx`**: The entry point. It sets up the React app and routing.
    -   **`App.jsx`**: The main layout component. It handles the routing between Login and Chat pages.

### 📄 Pages (`src/pages/`)
-   **`LoginPage.jsx`**:
    -   Simple form to enter a username.
    -   Calls the backend API to create/get the user.
    -   Saves the username to `localStorage`.
-   **`ChatPage.jsx`**:
    -   The main container for the chat interface.
    -   Holds the state for the `currentChat` (who you are talking to).
    -   Renders `Sidebar` and `ChatWindow`.

### 🧩 Components (`src/components/`)
-   **`Sidebar.jsx`**:
    -   **Lists Users & Groups**: Fetches them from the API.
    -   **Last Message Preview**: Polls the API to show the latest message and time.
    -   **Group Creation**: Modal to create new groups.
    -   **Logout**: Clears storage and refreshes.
-   **`ChatWindow.jsx`**: **The Core Chat UI**.
    -   **WebSocket Connection**: Connects to `ws://localhost:8000...` when a chat is selected.
    -   **Message List**: Displays messages with bubbles (Purple for you, Grey for others).
    -   **Input Area**: Text box, file attachment, and location sharing buttons.
    -   **Read Receipts**: Sends `read_receipt` events when you view messages and displays Blue Ticks.

---

## 🔄 How It All Connects

1.  **Login**: `LoginPage` -> API (`views.py`) -> Database (`models.py`).
2.  **Select Chat**: `Sidebar` -> Sets `currentChat` state.
3.  **Connect**: `ChatWindow` -> `ws://` -> `asgi.py` -> `routing.py` -> `ChatConsumer` (`consumers.py`).
4.  **Send Message**: `ChatWindow` -> WebSocket -> `ChatConsumer` -> Database.
5.  **Receive Message**: Database -> `ChatConsumer` -> WebSocket -> `ChatWindow` (Update UI).
